  "body": {
    "focus": "Pass chat prompts to the claude and codex CLIs after an end-of-options marker\n\nRoot cause: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts buildArgs puts the raw prompt where the CLI option parser reads it (claude ['-p', req.prompt, ...]; codex ['exec', '--json', ...auto, req.prompt] and the resume variant), so a prompt starting with '-' is parsed as an option.\n\nFix intent: both argv builders hand the prompt to the CLI so it can never be read as an option, for claude and codex, new and resumed turns; every other argument keeps its meaning.",
    "producesLld": false,
    "commit": "ec0dd3c7",
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "s1",
        "passed": true
      }
    ],
    "summary": "The chat's claude and codex argv builders now put every flag first and the prompt last, after '--', for new and resumed turns, so a prompt starting with '-' reaches the CLI as the prompt. Verified against the real claude CLI: without '--' a '- MED: ...' prompt fails with \"unknown option\"; with '--' it is read as the prompt. New test 65cb63f7 in cli-adapter.test.ts fails without the fix and passes with it.",
    "testRecord": {
